        kind: 'faded',
        text: 'An operator has 40,000 secondary substations. It plans to replace about 600 a year on condition, and must build about 1,800 new or upsized stations a year for reinforcement and new connections. One crew builds or replaces about three stations a week, over 46 working weeks. A study shows that 30% of the stations due for replacement sit in streets that also need reinforcement within five years.',
