        reveal: 'Total: 600 + 1,800 = 2,400 stations a year. One crew: 3 × 46 = 138 a year, so 2,400 / 138 ≈ 17.4, roughly 18 crews.\n\nBundling: 30% of 600 = 180 replacements can be done as part of reinforcement jobs. That removes about 180 jobs, 1.3 crews, and gives those streets a bigger station once instead of twice. The harder question is whether 18 crews exist at all, so standard designs and training count as much as the budget.',
